menu "WiFi Dap web server (HTTP / WebSocket)"

    config BIRDIEBOT_WEB_AUTH
        bool "Enable Web UI/API token authentication"
        default n
        help
            When enabled, the WebSocket endpoint (/ws) and the JSON HTTP API
            (/api, and future /api/ota/upload) require the pairing token
            (docs/protocol.md §1/§5):

              - WS: ?token=<token> in the connect URL and/or the first frame
                {"module":0,"cmd":0,"token":"<token>"} (SYSTEM cmd 0 AUTH);
              - HTTP: Authorization: Bearer <token> (or ?token=);
              - Host/Origin headers are validated to block DNS-rebinding.

            This option only protects the web management surface (HTTP port 80:
            /ws, /api, /api/ota/upload).  It does NOT protect TCP 3240
            (USBIP/WS-DAP/elaphureLink) nor TCP 1346 (UART TCP bridge): those
            stay unauthenticated and must be disabled (their own Kconfig) or
            kept on a trusted LAN (docs/security-review-web.md P1-1/P1-3).

            When disabled (default) the token check is compiled out and the
            device runs in laboratory mode: log in only from a trusted LAN.
            Host/Origin validation is ALWAYS active (independent of this
            option, see BIRDIEBOT_WEB_ALLOWED_ORIGIN).

    config BIRDIEBOT_WEB_TOKEN
        string "Fixed pairing token (empty = generate a random one at boot)"
        depends on BIRDIEBOT_WEB_AUTH
        default ""
        help
            Fixed pairing token (the "pair code" shown to the user).  It must
            be URL-safe: no spaces, '&', '%', '?', '#' or '/'.  Max 256 chars.

            When empty, a random 128-bit token (32 hex chars) is generated on
            the first boot and persisted in the wt_nvs partition (namespace
            "web_auth", key "token"), so it stays stable across reboots
            (security review P1-4; a legacy 8-hex token is rotated once).  The
            token is printed on the serial console at start-up:
                W (xxx) web_auth: Web auth ENABLED; pairing token: <32 hex> (...)
            Erase the wt_nvs partition (or the "web_auth" namespace) to rotate
            the generated token.

    config BIRDIEBOT_WEB_ALLOWED_ORIGIN
        string "Extra allowed Origin/Host entries (comma separated)"
        default ""
        help
            Comma-separated allow-list for the ALWAYS-ON Host/Origin check
            (security review P1-2: this check is independent from the token
            auth because browsers can open cross-origin WebSockets without a
            CORS preflight, and DNS rebinding works without any token), e.g.
                "http://192.168.1.1:8080,https://dap.local"
            Each entry is either a full origin (scheme://host[:port]) or a
            bare hostname.

            - Host header check: the request must carry a Host that is an IP
              literal, an entry from this list, or CONFIG_LWIP_LOCAL_HOSTNAME.
              This blocks DNS-rebinding hostnames (an attacker-controlled DNS
              name resolving to the device IP is rejected).
            - Origin header check: when a browser sends Origin it must be
              same-origin with Host, or match an entry from this list.

            Accessing the device through its IP (the documented way,
            docs/protocol.md §1) needs no entry.  Accessing it through a
            hostname (e.g. the mDNS name "dap.local", or a reverse-proxy
            name) requires adding that name here, e.g.
                CONFIG_BIRDIEBOT_WEB_ALLOWED_ORIGIN="http://dap.local"
            Requests with a non-IP, non-allow-listed Host or with a
            cross-origin Origin are rejected (HTTP 403; WS handshake closed)
            even in laboratory mode.

endmenu
